WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.792
The saved Week 14 plan names an EENT lab and says the course begins a zero-feedback standard. The specific station document was not yet available in the saved school view, so these are original practice stations based only on the visible objectives.
保存的第14周计划列出眼耳鼻喉实验，并说明课程开始采用零反馈标准。保存的学校页面中具体站点文件尚未开放，因此以下是根据可见目标编写的原创练习站。

00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:31.176
A no-prompt run tests whether the learner notices, prioritizes and explains. It is not a reason to permit preventable harm. The instructor retains a safety-interruption role; the learner receives coaching and correction after the run.
无提示演练测试学习者能否察觉、排序并解释。它不是允许可预防伤害发生的理由。教官仍保留安全中断职责；指导和纠正应在情景结束后进行。

00:00:31.176 --> 00:00:46.152
Before the clock begins, agree on the safe simulation boundaries, available equipment and stop word. During the run, the observer gives no hints; the learner must verbalize the reasoning that would otherwise remain invisible.
计时前先确认安全模拟边界、可用设备和停止口令。演练过程中观察者不提供提示；学习者必须把原本可能未说出口的推理讲出来。

00:00:46.152 --> 00:01:04.032
When a safety issue requires interruption, stop the clock, correct the immediate hazard and record the point. Resume only if the instructor decides the simulation remains useful. This is an original coaching method, not a claim about the school’s exact formal protocol.
若出现需要干预的安全问题，应停表、消除即时危险并记录节点。是否继续由教官判断是否仍有训练价值。这是原创教学方法，不代表学校正式流程的确切规定。

00:01:04.032 --> 00:01:21.576
During the run, write short observable notes: “kept child upright,” “asked for a forced mouth exam,” “started rinse before product label arrived,” or “released nose pressure twice.” Avoid vague notes such as “bad confidence” or “not ready.”
演练时记录简短、可观察的事实，例如“让孩子保持直立”“要求强行检查口腔”“在产品标签送到前已开始冲洗”或“反复松开鼻部压力”。避免“信心差”“不够准备”等含糊评价。

00:01:21.576 --> 00:01:40.992
The accessible BCPEG page 80 groups deficiencies by likely impact and includes sequence, safety and critical reporting. The unseen pages 274–276 may add criteria; do not treat this worksheet as their substitute or assign an official passing score.
可访问的BCPEG第80页按可能影响对缺陷分类，并包含顺序、安全和关键报告内容。未见的274–276页可能另有标准；不要把本工作表当作替代品，也不要给出官方通过分数。

00:01:40.992 --> 00:01:54.432
Use simulation props only. Do not practise medication administration, invasive airway actions, eye-object extraction or other procedures outside a supervised school station and current authorization.
只使用模拟道具。不要在受监督的学校站点和现行授权之外，练习给药、侵入性气道操作、拔除眼内异物或其他操作。

00:01:54.432 --> 00:02:10.608
Plan the route and roles before the patient contact: who is leading, who obtains equipment, who communicates with the receiving team and who monitors the scene. Clear role assignment prevents a single learner from losing the whole patient while focusing on one local detail.
接触患者前先规划路径和分工：谁负责领导、谁取设备、谁联系接收团队、谁监控现场。明确分工可避免学习者因专注局部细节而忽略患者整体。

00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:28.128
Scenario: the child remains awake, drools, leans forward and becomes agitated when an examiner approaches with a tongue depressor. The learner should identify the airway threat and stop the unnecessary examination rather than trying to prove a diagnosis.
情景：儿童仍清醒、流涎、前倾；考官拿压舌板靠近时，孩子变得烦躁。学习者应识别气道风险并停止不必要的检查，而不是尝试证明某个诊断。

00:02:28.128 --> 00:02:47.256
A strong independent response explains why the child stays upright, what observations can be obtained without provocation, how early transport/support is organized and which change would trigger immediate escalation. Do not give medication or perform a procedure simply to fill station time.
有力的独立应答应解释为何让孩子保持直立、如何在不刺激的情况下观察、怎样及早安排转运和支援，以及什么变化会触发立即升级。不要为了填满站点时间而随意给药或操作。

00:02:47.256 --> 00:03:06.768
During the run, the child stops resisting and becomes quiet. The learner must not use silence as the only improvement measure. Look again at responsiveness, speech, respiratory effort, colour and air movement; a fatigued child may look less active while becoming more dangerous.
演练中，儿童不再挣扎并安静下来。学习者不能只凭安静就判断好转。要重新观察反应、说话、呼吸做功、肤色和气流；疲劳的儿童可能活动减少，但风险反而增加。

00:03:06.768 --> 00:03:23.040
State the trend aloud, describe the likely airway risk and use the current service escalation pathway. Do not force an oral examination to resolve uncertainty; uncertainty is a reason to escalate, not a reason to provoke the airway.
应口述变化趋势，说明可能的气道风险，并使用现行服务升级流程。不要为了消除不确定性而强行检查口腔；不确定性是升级处置的理由，不是刺激气道的理由。

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:39.768
Scenario: a worker has bleach splashed in one eye, and saline has not arrived. The learning objective is to prevent delay: start suitable clean-water irrigation while another responder identifies the product and contacts the appropriate support resource.
情景：工人一只眼睛被漂白剂溅到，盐水尚未到位。学习目标是避免延误：先用适当清洁水冲洗，同时让另一位救援人员识别产品并联系适当支援。

00:03:39.768 --> 00:03:57.312
Protect the responder and prevent runoff from contaminating the other eye or surrounding people. Use a gentle controlled flow. Continue according to the chemical-specific advice; do not neutralize the chemical or stop solely because the school timer reached 15 minutes.
保护救援人员，并避免流出液污染另一只眼或周围人员。采用轻柔、可控的水流。按化学物质专属意见继续冲洗；不要尝试中和化学物质，也不要只因学校计时达到15分钟就停止。

00:03:57.312 --> 00:04:15.648
In the school rehearsal, verbalize the specified “at least 15 minutes” saline target. In actual readiness reasoning, distinguish the target from an endpoint: start clean fluid promptly, contact CliniCall as required and follow exposure-specific guidance.
学校演练中，要口述指定的“至少15分钟”盐水冲洗目标。实际执业推理中则要区分目标时长与停止点：及时开始清洁液冲洗，按要求联系CliniCall，并遵循具体暴露指导。

00:04:15.648 --> 00:04:32.304
The observer should note both parts: did the learner know the school criterion, and did they avoid a harmful delay when saline was not immediately available? This resolves the apparent conflict without erasing either the school exercise or current service guidance.
观察者应记录两部分：学习者是否知道学校标准；盐水未立即到位时，是否避免了有害延误。这样可以化解表面冲突，同时保留学校练习和现行服务指导。

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:49.008
Scenario: after a workshop accident, a small object is visible at the eye and the patient reports pain with blurred vision. Do not use forceps, press on the eye, remove the object or perform a lengthy visual-acuity sequence before transport planning.
情景：工坊事故后，眼部可见小异物，患者诉眼痛和视物模糊。不要使用镊子、压迫眼睛、拔除异物，也不要在安排转运前进行冗长的视力检查。

00:04:49.008 --> 00:05:03.936
Protect the eye using an appropriate rigid shield if available and prevent movement of the object. Assess for the same mechanism’s head or facial injury, monitor the patient and arrange prompt specialist assessment under current guidance.
如有合适硬质护罩，应保护眼睛并避免异物移动。评估同一机制造成的头面部损伤，监测患者，并按现行指导安排及时专科评估。

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:19.656
Scenario: a patient with a nosebleed is leaning back and repeatedly checking whether bleeding has stopped. Guide the patient to sit upright and lean slightly forward; demonstrate the correct compression point and maintain pressure without intermittent checking.
情景：鼻出血患者后仰并不断查看是否止血。应指导患者坐直并略微前倾；示范正确按压位置，并持续按压，不要间断查看。

00:05:19.656 --> 00:05:36.816
Ask about trauma, blood-thinning medicines and bleeding disorders while pressure is maintained. Do not focus solely on the nose: assess airway, amount of blood loss, vital signs, symptoms and relevant chronic conditions, then follow the current pathway.
持续按压时，询问创伤、抗凝药物和出血性疾病。不能只关注鼻子：还要评估气道、失血量、生命体征、症状和相关慢性病，并遵循现行流程。

00:05:36.816 --> 00:05:52.152
Use an original practice case, not a hidden school case. Start a five-minute timer only after the learner has heard the dispatch and scene information. The goal is to structure a usable record efficiently, not to reward typing speed.
使用原创练习案例，而不是学校隐藏案例。学习者听完派遣和现场信息后再启动五分钟计时。目标是高效整理可用记录，而不是奖励打字速度。

00:05:52.152 --> 00:06:08.952
After the timer, check whether a reader can reconstruct what happened, what changed, why an action was taken, what response followed and what remains unresolved. Record the actual completion time separately from completeness; one does not prove the other.
计时结束后，检查读者能否还原事件经过、变化、采取行动的理由、后续反应和未解决问题。完成时间与记录完整性应分开核查；一个不能证明另一个。

00:06:08.952 --> 00:06:27.648
The saved plan asks for a Sunday written self-assessment using Appendix G and three weak points for Week 16 remediation. The official appendix was not available in the source set. This is an original three-gap preparation tool, not Appendix G and not a substitute for the school form.
保存的计划要求周日使用Appendix G做书面自评，并提出三个弱项供第16周补救。现有资料中未找到官方附录。本工具是原创的三弱项准备模板，不是Appendix G，也不能替代学校表格。

00:06:27.648 --> 00:06:46.896
Phrase gaps as observable actions: “I did not state the child’s position as a risk cue before planning transport,” or “I delayed irrigation while waiting for saline.” Then choose one repeated drill and a clear success observation. Avoid labels about character or confidence.
将弱项写成可观察行为，例如“安排转运前未把儿童体位说成风险线索”或“等待盐水期间延误了冲洗”。然后选择重复练习，并设定清晰的成功观察点。避免对性格或信心贴标签。

00:06:46.896 --> 00:06:59.664
Start with the learner’s account, then compare it with the observer’s factual notes. Ask what the learner expected to happen, what actually happened, and which alternative explanation or change they considered.
先听学习者复述，再与观察者的事实记录对照。询问学习者预期发生什么、实际发生什么，以及考虑过哪些替代解释或变化。

00:06:59.664 --> 00:07:14.328
Choose only a few high-value practice targets. Re-run the scenario so the learner can demonstrate the changed behavior. This reduces the gap between recognizing a mistake in discussion and performing the safe action under time pressure.
只选择少数高价值练习目标。重新演练情景，让学习者实际展示行为变化。这样能缩小“复盘时知道错误”和“时间压力下做出安全行动”之间的差距。

00:07:14.328 --> 00:07:32.352
Do not collapse all EENT calls into one generic exam. The right priority depends on the threat: airway compromise, ongoing chemical exposure, globe penetration or hemorrhage. State the reason for the first action and the observation that will change your plan.
不要把所有眼耳鼻喉事件都简化成同一种检查。正确优先事项取决于威胁：气道受损、持续化学暴露、眼球穿透或出血。说明首要行动的理由，以及什么观察结果会改变计划。

00:07:32.352 --> 00:07:46.776
The official lab sheet and Appendix G must be checked when the school releases them. Until then, use these original stations to build independent reasoning, accurate PCR habits and a concrete list of practice needs.
学校开放官方实验说明和Appendix G后，应再核对其内容。在此之前，可用这些原创站点练习独立推理、准确记录PCR，并列出具体练习需求。
